    <briefdescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="classthrust_1_1discard__iterator" kindref="compound">discard_iterator</ref></computeroutput> is an iterator which represents a special kind of pointer that ignores values written to it upon dereference. This iterator is useful for ignoring the output of certain algorithms without wasting memory capacity or bandwidth. <computeroutput><ref refid="classthrust_1_1discard__iterator" kindref="compound">discard_iterator</ref></computeroutput> may also be used to count the size of an algorithm&apos;s output which may not be known a priori. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The following code snippet demonstrates how to use <computeroutput><ref refid="classthrust_1_1discard__iterator" kindref="compound">discard_iterator</ref></computeroutput> to ignore one of the output ranges of reduce_by_key</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">#include<sp/>&lt;thrust/iterator/discard_iterator.h&gt;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">#include<sp/>&lt;thrust/reduce.h&gt;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">#include<sp/>&lt;thrust/device_vector.h&gt;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">int<sp/>main()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>thrust::device_vector&lt;int&gt;<sp/>keys{1,<sp/>3,<sp/>3,<sp/>3,<sp/>2,<sp/>2,<sp/>1};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>thrust::device_vector&lt;int&gt;<sp/>values{9,<sp/>8,<sp/>7,<sp/>6,<sp/>5,<sp/>4,<sp/>3};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>thrust::device_vector&lt;int&gt;<sp/>result(4);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>//<sp/>we<sp/>are<sp/>only<sp/>interested<sp/>in<sp/>the<sp/>reduced<sp/>values</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>//<sp/>use<sp/>discard_iterator<sp/>to<sp/>ignore<sp/>the<sp/>output<sp/>keys</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>thrust::reduce_by_key(keys.begin(),<sp/>keys.end(),</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>values.begin(),</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>thrust::make_discard_iterator(),</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>result.begin());</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>//<sp/>result<sp/>is<sp/>now<sp/>[9,<sp/>21,<sp/>9,<sp/>3]</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>return<sp/>0;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
